<title>SPAIN: Spain's Bankinter H1 net up 8.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Bankinter H1 net up 8.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half of 1997.</p>
<p>(in billions of pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit	 9.38    up 8.01 pct</p>
<p> Pretax profit		    13.69    up 8.95 pct</p>
<p> Ordinary income			 36.34    vs   31.16</p>
<p> Operating income			20.28    vs   16.60</p>
<p> Net commissions			   9.23   vs    8.17</p>
<p> Financial income			  8.69   vs    4.40</p>
<p> Operating costs			  14.78   vs   13.00</p>
<p>    -personnel costs		     8.79   vs    8.18</p>
<p>    -general, administrative costs   5.98   vs    4.82</p>
<p> Depreciation				1.41   vs    1.35</p>
<p> Other operating income		122.00   vs (224.00)</p>
<p> Gains on group transactions	   73.00  vs    1.00</p>
<p> Net extraordinary losses		(5.41) vs (999.00)</p>
<p> Corporate income tax		     4.31  vs    3.88</p>
<p> Return on assets (percent)	     1.11  vs    0.98</p>
<p> Return on equity (percent)	    18.79  vs   17.73</p>
<p> Total assets			   1,802.88  vs 1,671.39</p>
<p>Note - Losses are in brackets. Full name is Banco Intercontinental Espanol SA.</p>
</text>
